Very nice. I've loved PyPy as a way to run Python faster, but it only got to Python 3.12 this September, and that's still beta (
https://pypy.org/posts/2026/10/pypy-v801-release.html
). That's about 3 years after CPython's 3.12. JIT in CPython itself seems on-again, off-again, so great news that an external approach might be able to take up some slack.
